Tenali Rama and the Stolen Mangoes (Raw Story)

One day, King Krishnadevaraya noticed that some of his favorite mangoes were missing from the royal garden.

He was very upset and suspected that one of the servants had stolen them.

The king asked all the servants, but no one admitted the truth.

Tenali Rama stepped forward and said, “Your Majesty, I can find the thief.”

He gave each servant a stick and said, “Keep this stick with you tonight. If you are the thief, your stick will grow longer by morning.”

All the servants took their sticks and went home.

The guilty servant became very scared. He thought, “If my stick grows, I will be caught!”

So, during the night, he cut his stick shorter.

The next morning, all the servants returned with their sticks.

Tenali Rama looked at them carefully and immediately pointed to one servant.

“This is the thief!” he said.

The king asked, “How do you know?”

Tenali smiled and said, “Because his stick is shorter than the others.”

The servant realized his mistake and confessed.

The king praised Tenali Rama for his cleverness.

💖 Moral:

Truth always comes out.
